<title>USA: Conseco sets 5 million share buyback plan.</title>
<headline>Conseco sets 5 million share buyback plan.</headline>
<dateline>CARMEL, Ind. 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Conseco Inc said Friday it set a new program to repurchase up to five million share of common stock in open market or negotiated transactions.</p>
<p>Conseco also said it completed its previous five million share repurchase program.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe that Conseco's stock is undervalued and that purchases by the company at these levels will benefit our long-term shareholders,&quot; Conseco Chairman Stephen Hilbert said in a statement.</p>
<p>Conseco is a financial services organization. Through its subsidiaries, Conseco provides supplemental health insurance, retirement annuities and universal life insurance.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
